From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:29:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the UART3, UART5 and UART6
 controllers

Boards bring out more A733 UARTs than UART0, UART2 and UART4 on their pin
headers, but the SoC dtsi describes only those.

Add UART3 at 0x02503000, UART5 at 0x02505000 and UART6 at 0x02506000,
DesignWare APB UARTs like the existing ones, with their bus clocks and
resets. On the A733 the UARTs are 4 KiB apart. Add the pin groups with
which UART3 reaches the Cubie A7S header J11: TX/RX on PD16/PD17
(function 7) and on PJ22/PJ23 (function 4). These are the pins of TWI2
and TWI7, so a board uses either function on a pin pair, and the two
groups are separate. The nodes are disabled; a board enables them.

Not covered: DMA requests, and RTS/CTS of UART3: RTS on PD14 is a plain
GPIO pin on the header, and CTS on PD15 is not wired. UART5 and UART6
have no pin groups: no pin of either reaches a header on this board, and
the pins they could use carry other functions (Ethernet, microSD, camera
connector).

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the nodes enabled in a copy of the DTB,
UART3 on PD16/PD17, UART5 and UART6 probe as 16550A.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 47 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 47 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index d0677503b443..726171bfe6b8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -629,6 +629,20 @@ uart2_rts_cts_pb_pins: uart2-rts-cts-pb-pins {
 				function = "uart2";
 			};
 
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			uart3_pd_pins: uart3-pd-pins {
+				pins = "PD16", "PD17";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <7>;
+				function = "uart3";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			uart3_pj_pins: uart3-pj-pins {
+				pins = "PJ22", "PJ23";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <4>;
+				function = "uart3";
+			};
+
 			/omit-if-no-ref/
 			uart4_pj_pins: uart4-pj-pins {
 				pins = "PJ24", "PJ25";
@@ -692,6 +706,17 @@ uart2: serial@2502000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		uart3: serial@2503000 {
+			compatible = "snps,dw-apb-uart";
+			reg = <0x02503000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 5 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			reg-shift = <2>;
+			reg-io-width = <4>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_UART3>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_UART3>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		uart4: serial@2504000 {
 			compatible = "snps,dw-apb-uart";
 			reg = <0x02504000 0x400>;
@@ -703,6 +728,28 @@ uart4: serial@2504000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		uart5: serial@2505000 {
+			compatible = "snps,dw-apb-uart";
+			reg = <0x02505000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 7 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			reg-shift = <2>;
+			reg-io-width = <4>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_UART5>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_UART5>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		uart6: serial@2506000 {
+			compatible = "snps,dw-apb-uart";
+			reg = <0x02506000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 8 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			reg-shift = <2>;
+			reg-io-width = <4>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_UART6>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_UART6>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		i2c0: i2c@2510000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-i2c",
 				     "allwinner,sun8i-v536-i2c",
